        {
          "id": "5c5c1a66-4cd0-4a41-8f11-68e9cc956b91",
          "listId": "5969e69c-fe41-4634-85b5-3cd8c9380974",
          "title": "Support quick deletion",
          "description": "\nallowable in configuration, default is off.\n\nWhen writting the user input (answer) \"!!\" (careful that ! is the command to quit the session, !! if detected should not quit the study session ) it should add into a to-remove queue which will be ignored when studying. Then create a js queue which if if not empty whenever running maid ses should indicate the absolute path to find and review for true removal. (Also remind that maid cleanp command) it should also remind if exists any term with feedback in it\n\nfrom the options when removing:\n\nContinue to next question\nTry the question again\nProvide feedback about this term\n[new: move to deletion queue]\n[new: force remove] #this would force removing it from the things\nRate this flashcard\nReset deck progress\nQuit the entire session\n\n\n\nThere should be also a maid cleanup for removing all the terms that are on that to be deleted queue if running like maid cleanup --backup will remove them but move them to backup folder\n\nAlso create a logs.txt file in data where each time that the user removes or completes a deck, provides feedback then the actionis logged, also usage stats (useful for future improvement) this should be configurable in settings.json\n",
          "labels": [],
          "checkboxes": [],
          "comments": []
        },
        {
          "id": "10eb0e8d-4e25-4bc9-8676-bd6b2ec51aec",
          "listId": "5969e69c-fe41-4634-85b5-3cd8c9380974",
          "title": "Clean and Organize Automated Decks",
          "description": "To be both added and modified from processed.\nReduce manually\nAdd the chinese description (and translated answer) \n\nThe idea of the chinese description is making it a bit tougher toanswer. That would be entire different folders.\n\nTo test, actually read and then decrease, have a kanban for this on the own esresearch\n\n",
          "labels": [],
