          "listId": "5969e69c-fe41-4634-85b5-3cd8c9380974",
          "title": "Last Session Learned Queue",
          "description": "to ensure learning. whenever a flashcard is learnt, using a similar code pattern to before on create a queue on src/user_data/review_decks.json under index of [date]: {revised: false, decks: List[Dict]} for the cards and accumulate everything learnt  (successfully learnt, not just seen cards) on that date. \n\nThen when running maid ses or maid fses it should appears the days decks for today and last session so that we can review all decks learnt last session or today. Store up to 5 different dates, after 5 dates remove the oldest one\n\n",
          "labels": [],
          "checkboxes": [],
          "comments": []
        },
        {
          "id": "6d9e3665-3026-42c2-82ea-fdc644e3936a",
          "listId": "5969e69c-fe41-4634-85b5-3cd8c9380974",
          "title": "Fix indentation for solutions",
          "description": "Fix indentation for flashcards storage\nI believe either when scanning for flashcards from mrkdowns files it is not storing the indentation for both ouside and inside of codeblocks inside of ``` pre blocks. Which is important because without tab indentation, or spaces at the start, there is likely a regex messing it up.  doesn't work properly and cant show the code logics . Fix that by including indentations when scanning inside of code blocks.\n",
          "labels": [],
          "checkboxes": [],
          "comments": []
        },
